{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqfnyddvxdj","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"Kept note context edges now drive structBoost retrieval after CL-2d daemon fix is live","summary":"RESOLVED (2026-06-15, supersedes note-mqfn8l1hpiw): the note↔note kept-edge structBoost inertness is FIXED and live. CL-2d (commit 574b45b, merged to main as 356ad16, daemon restarted pid 84223→56853 at 20:25Z) made two daemon changes: (1) buildGraph (daemon.js ~L1609) populates a note's context_deps from its JUDGED-KEPT context edges (kind=context, edgeWeight!==0, mirroring the task-side depRefs filter — raw weight-0 autowire candidates excluded), so the structBoost reranker boosts judged neighbors; (2) lib/overlay.js emitDiff emits a new edge_promoted event + lib/graph-store.js setPrevState clones edges so keepEdge's in-place weight promotion persists across reload. Verified: 19/19 tests on a throwaway daemon (kept edge 0.408→0.453, structBoost 0.045; weight-0 candidate no boost); the judge cold-loaded the live 670-node/3087-edge store under both old+new code and got byte-identical edge sets (0 differing, backMiss=0) — backward-compatible. Net: the CL Zonoid arm's LLM-judged wiring now actually influences retrieval ranking (not just dedup), so it genuinely tests structured memory vs flat FAISS. This also improves the live product's note↔note edge retrieval generally, not just the bench.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-15T20:26:18.307Z","vec":[-0.10564343631267548,0.013820328749716282,-0.04137324169278145,-0.0029765365179628134,0.06795851141214371,-0.030192511156201363,-0.012120800092816353,0.020994218066334724,-0.017510073259472847,0.004318800289183855,0.004540819674730301,0.02086576633155346,0.026048172265291214,-0.02635078877210617,-0.0036634025163948536,-0.0008304556249640882,0.14656101167201996,-0.017777197062969208,-0.043856605887413025,0.02900305949151516,0.02002602443099022,-0.05270955339074135,0.006024288944900036,-0.010412980802357197,0.0439162626862525